course: dictionary
lesson: 4208
title: Gothic: old, spooky or stylish?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need context to know which one the writer means. In «The front door has “Mole End” painted, in Gothic lettering, over the bell-pull», the words lettering and front door tell you Gothic means old-fashioned, with pointed letters.
explain: Now read the words around the word. A gothic novel, a crumbling house, a storm and candlelight all point to a spooky story. Those clues tell you gothic means spooky and mysterious, not old churches or dark clothes.
explain: Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does «The front door has “Mole End” painted, in old-fashioned, pointed lettering» still make sense? If yes, you have the right meaning.
fact: Gothic means in the style of many churches and cathedrals built in Europe from about 1150 to 1500.
fact: Gothic buildings have pointed arches, tall spires and big stained-glass windows.
fact: Gothic stories are spooky tales with old castles, ghosts, dark nights and mystery.
fact: Notre-Dame in Paris and Westminster Abbey in London are famous Gothic cathedrals.
fact: Gothic can also mean of the Goths, an old Germanic people, or their language. Goth, in informal speech, means a style of dress and music with black clothes and dark make-up.
exercise: «The front door has “Mole End” painted, in Gothic lettering, over the bell-pull.» What does Gothic lettering mean here? | *Old-fashioned, pointed letters | Letters made of gold paint | Letters that are very small | Letters written in another language
exercise: A story has ghosts, dark nights and an old castle. What kind of story is it? | *A gothic story | A recipe for cakes | A sports report | A map of a city
exercise: Which building has pointed arches, tall spires and big stained-glass windows? | A wooden garden shed | A tent on a campsite | *A Gothic cathedral | A modern shopping centre
test: «The old house had a gothic mood, with a storm outside and candles flickering.» What does gothic suggest here? | Very noisy and busy | Bright and cheerful | Hot and sunny | *Spooky and mysterious
test: Which of these is a famous Gothic cathedral? | *Westminster Abbey | Hadrian's Wall | Buckingham Palace | Eiffel Tower
exam: Gothic has more than one meaning. Which meaning fits a person in black clothes and dark make-up who listens to dark music? | *A dark style of dress and music, informal (Goth) | A spooky story set in a castle | Pointed arches in an old church | The language of an old Germanic people
